From 9fda6342d8fce2d26c04ea58f1e5db0750c1ce41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaTor <deltator@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:06:25 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] conflux: add ConfluxProbeLog diagnostics for
 measured-throughput selection

The measured-throughput set-selection policy (ConfluxSetSelection 4) decides
which set a new stream uses from real download throughput that is otherwise
invisible, which makes it hard to tell whether the mechanism is behaving as
intended. Add a new "confluxmthr" log domain (a real new LD_CONFLUXMTHR bit)
that records every step of the mechanism:

  - a set's measurement window being opened;
  - every window roll: elapsed time, delivered bytes, raw bytes/sec and the
    smoothed estimate (trusted, or decayed when traffic was too low);
  - each candidate set's throughput and selection weight on a pick;
  - the pick summary (max bps, floor, total weight, random roll) and the set
    that was chosen;
  - one startup line noting whether the active policy really is mode 4.

A new torrc option ConfluxProbeLog (0-2) controls it: 0 = off (default),
1 = log the mechanism alongside tor's normal logs, 2 = log only the
mechanism and suppress tor's other log lines (errors are always kept) so the
mechanism can be verified in isolation. Level 2 is implemented with a flag
checked at the top of logv(); it is set from options_init_logs() only when
the options are really being applied (never during validation).

The mechanism lines use LD_CONFLUXMTHR, so they can also be selected per
target without suppressing anything, e.g. "Log [confluxmthr]notice file
conflux-probe.log". The domain is documented in tor.1.txt, the option is
added to DELTATOR-CHANGES.md, and both shipped torrc files set it to 0 with
a commented diagnostic example.
